/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 45 0 R
/T (provides read and write access to an internal register map. The register map is 32768 registers deep and 8 bits wide, addressed by a 15-bit address field. The design must support both single-byte and multi-byte \(burst, auto-incrementing\) accesses, and must be able to present read data back to the master with no more)
/E (provides read and write access to an internal register map. The register map is 32768 registers deep and 8 bits wide, addressed by a 15-bit address field. The design must support both single-byte and multi-byte \(burst, auto-incrementing\) accesses, and must be able to present read data back to the master with no more)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
